WP06 security and no-claim proof

Negative cases covered by tests:
- Inventory adapter rows keep runtimeState=notClaimed.
- Inventory adapter rows keep foregroundState=notClaimed.
- Inventory adapter rows keep runningDurationMs=0.
- Inventory adapter rows keep foregroundDurationMs=0.
- Matching display labels alone do not merge, preventing weak-name promotion.
- Launcher manifest inventory becomes an installed nativeGame candidate only,
  not a gameplay/session/foreground claim.
- Registry/shortcut dedupe requires shared strong identity refs.

Explicitly not claimed:
- raw executable path display in parent UI;
- live Windows registry access;
- shell-link parsing;
- executable metadata/signature/hash collection;
- launcher manifest crawling;
- journal replay stability;
- enforcement or broad blocking;
- UI safety for malicious metadata.
